            <ArticleTitle>Early stent thrombosis because of stent dislodgement in a coronary artery aneurysm.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1759-61</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Stent thrombosis is one of the most feared complications after coronary stenting, because it often presents in a catastrophic way, triggering death or acute myocardial infarction. Previous studies report mechanical risk factors of stent thrombosis such as stent underexpansion and vessel dissection. This is a case report of early stent thrombosis associated with bare metal stent dislodgement because of dissolution of a mural thrombus in an unappreciated coronary artery aneurysm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
